The dish is a square white plate, probably about 22 cm across. It looks like roughly 8-10 strips of cooked bacon piled together, covering about 10 x 8 cm.

Cooked bacon runs about 8 g per strip and about 540 kcal per 100 g. These strips look glazed or sugared, which would add some calories. Nine strips at roughly 8 g each comes to about 70 g, though the pile could be closer to 60 g. At that weight the energy is about 350 kcal. The strips look thin and crisp, so I'll settle on 65 g and about 330 kcal.

